Everything is ok to the people at MW!

@Kerem
To add to Lewis's comment.  
You may not find the earliest Wordplay columns linked to the puzzle when you press the i for info from the games app. To find those, go to xwordinfo.com, find your puzzle and look for the link from there.

@max Ta for asking this question. I really love the NYT crossword but my least favourite clue has to be anything indicating that TA TA is how us Brits say goodbye. Perhaps TA TA was a British farewell of old… but I lived there from birth until I was in my 20s and never once heard TA used to say goodbye - it was, however, frequently used as a quick thanks. 

In fact, I only learned that Americans understood it as a goodbye in my 30s when, after IMing “ta” to a US colleague multiple times over months of working together, he wrote to me “TIL that ‘ta’ means ‘thanks’. i thought it meant ‘bye’.”  Meaning he’d send something helpful my way, and then believed I was replying with a blunt “bye” rather than any gratitude. Hi Jim if you’re reading this. 

Anyway, seeing TAS clued as it was today brought me a lot of joy :) so, ta for that!

